{# MagicFront chrome-only layout — PANELS. Sibling of mff-chrome-only-header/footer.html.twig,
   selected by ?mff_chrome_only=accountPanel|basketPanel|mobileMenuPanel. The three share this file:
   what changes is WHICH panel the initializer emitted, not how it is painted, and only the scoped
   one carries globals — so the three `if`s below resolve to exactly one. The scaffolding the three
   chrome-only variants share lives in _mff-chrome-only-shell.html.twig.

   A panel is an overlay the visitor OPENS FROM THE HEADER: inside a whole shop page it is invisible
   by construction (`.offcanvas` ships hidden and translated off-screen), so the merchant edited it
   blind; painted ALONE it became a second window with no sign of where it came from. Here the header
   renders BEHIND, exactly as the storefront paints it, and the panel sits over it untranslated and
   visible — the screen the visitor sees with the panel open. The footer and the page body are not
   emitted: neither is being edited.

   The header is CONTEXT, not content: it is sealed into its own stacking context so the panel paints
   over it, and the whole wrapper is `inert`, which takes its clicks, its hovers, its drags, its focus
   and its place in the accessibility tree away in one go. Keying on `.mff-widget` was not enough and
   was actively wrong: that wrapper is emitted only by OUR macro, so with the back-office header
   toggle off the theme paints its own header and every link, dropdown and the hamburger stayed live
   under the dim — and the hamburger toggles the very offcanvas being edited. The editor filters its
   own events to the subtree it is editing too, but a "+" bar that lights up and does nothing is a
   promise the screen cannot keep.

   The panel is emitted HERE and only here: the parent layout's header block emits the three panels so
   our triggers have something to open, and `mffPanelOnly` turns that emission off on a scoped render —
   with both emitting, the panel was in the document twice under the same widget ids.

   The panel is NOT laid flat. `.offcanvas` ships fixed, and the pieces the panels position
   absolutely (the close button, the empty-cart block) are laid out against it — turned static they
   escaped to the viewport and spread across the whole screen. Only `visibility` and `transform` are
   undone, which is exactly what opening it does.

   The macro import is this template's own: Twig imports are template-local, and a block declared in a
   child does not inherit the parent's. Without it the macro call resolves to null and the panel is
   silently dropped — the screen renders white.

   The panel is emitted OUTSIDE `.commerce-content` on purpose: the store theme's `beforeJs` moves
   every `.offcanvas` it finds in there to `<body>` and leaves behind what does not hang from it —
   including the `MFF_WIDGET_START` markers the canvas reads. Out of its reach the panel never gets
   separated from its wrapper nor from its markers; its own script still re-anchors wrapper and panel
   to `<body>`, which is harmless.

   The CSS keys on `data-widget-family` for the versioned panels and on the bare family class for the
   v1s. A versioned family emits `widget-accountPanel--v2`, which a `.widget-accountPanel` selector does
   not match, so the rule died in silence when the panels went to @2; the attribute carries no version,
   so it cannot rot the same way. But the three v1 panels (the ones in production, and the ones the
   stores keep saved) carry no `data-widget-family`: keyed on it alone, Personalización painted the
   header under the dim and no panel at all (#7747). Their class carries no version either and is
   frozen with the published v1, so each one is named. Unlike `data-mff-el="section"`, both name the
   panel instead of a role 25 families share.

   El ASPA del cascarón (`data-mff-lock`) pierde los eventos de puntero: el guarda del lienzo ya
   bloqueaba su `data-bs-dismiss`, así que ofrecía cursor de mano para no hacer nada. Ahora el clic
   cae en el panel y lo selecciona, como cualquier otra zona bloqueada. El widget `panelClose` no
   lleva la marca y se sigue seleccionando para editarlo.

   The area AROUND the panel is DIMMED, and the dim has to be STRONG enough to be read as one. It
   started at 6% — 255,255,255 to 240,240,240 — which is no dim at all: the header behind looked as
   live as the panel, offered itself to be clicked and then answered nothing, because its pointer
   events are gone. A scrim is what says "this is the backdrop and the panel is the subject", so it
   sits where a modal's does. A background-color on `body` changes NOTHING (the theme paints above
   it). It is its own element rather than `body::before`, which belongs to the merchant's theme and
   would be clobbered here but nowhere else. It sits UNDER the panel, which is fixed and comes later
   in the document, and over the header, which is context. It takes no click. #}
{%- extends "Responsive/layouts/_mff-chrome-only-shell.html.twig" -%}
{%- import macrosCore.widget as widgetMacros -%}

{%- block chromeOnlyStyles -%}
    <style>
        .mff-panel-backdrop { position: relative; z-index: 0; }
        .mff-panel-backdrop .mff-add-widget-bar { display: none; }
        .mff-panel-dim {
            position: fixed;
            inset: 0;
            z-index: 1;
            background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
            pointer-events: none;
        }
        .offcanvas[data-widget-family],
        .offcanvas.widget-accountPanel,
        .offcanvas.widget-basketPanel,
        .offcanvas.widget-mobileMenuPanel {
            visibility: visible;
            transform: none;
            max-width: 100%;
        }
        .offcanvas-backdrop { display: none; }
        .offcanvas [data-bs-dismiss="offcanvas"][data-mff-lock] { pointer-events: none; }
    </style>
{%- endblock chromeOnlyStyles -%}

{% block wrapperClasses %} mff-panel-backdrop{% endblock wrapperClasses %}

{% block wrapperAttributes %} inert{% endblock wrapperAttributes %}

{%- block regionAbove -%}{{- block('header') -}}{%- endblock regionAbove -%}

{%- block afterWrapper -%}
    <div class="mff-panel-dim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    {%- if mffAccountPanelPages|default(null) -%}
        {{ widgetMacros.widgets({ pages: mffAccountPanelPages, version: version, widgetTemplateList: mffAccountPanelTemplateList, shared: mffShared|default({}) }) }}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if mffBasketPanelPages|default(null) -%}
        {{ widgetMacros.widgets({ pages: mffBasketPanelPages, version: version, widgetTemplateList: mffBasketPanelTemplateList, shared: mffShared|default({}) }) }}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if mffMobileMenuPanelPages|default(null) -%}
        {{ widgetMacros.widgets({ pages: mffMobileMenuPanelPages, version: version, widgetTemplateList: mffMobileMenuPanelTemplateList, shared: mffShared|default({}) }) }}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endblock afterWrapper -%}
